and WorkBuddy-Bench.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compute–Performance Trade-off.</span>
Figure <a href="#S4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 4 Analysis ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> compares performance and total compute on JobBench and WorkBuddy-Bench, counting all tokens spent before the final deliverable is submitted. Both evaluated <span id="S4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Harness<sup id="S4.p4.1.2.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.p4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">2</span></sup></span> configurations lie on the empirical Pareto frontier. With Gemini 3.5 Flash under OpenCode, increasing <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> raises gains over the base from <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.5</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.5</annotation></semantics></math> points on JobBench and from <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8.4</annotation></semantics></math> on WorkBuddy-Bench. ReasoningBank and Harness Scaling yield smaller gains, while Meta-Harness uses more compute than <span id="S4.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Harness<sup id="S4.p4.1.3.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.p4.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">2</span></sup></span> at <math id="S4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}5</annotation></semantics></math> for lower performance. This comparison includes both execution and improvement costs.</p>
</div>
