<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation Study.</span>
We ablate three components of <span id="S4.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Harness<sup id="S4.p5.1.2.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.p5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">2</span></sup></span>: (i) the harness improvement library of
§<a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 Harnessing-Level Recursion ‣ 2 Harness2 ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>, (ii) the scoped editor roles, and (iii) composition. Experiments are conducted on WorkBuddy-Bench, averaged over its
three domains, and on JobBench, with Gemini 3.5 Flash as the executor under the OpenCode
harness at <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that each component is isolated from the test-time
<span id="S4.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text">budget of §<a href="#S2.SS2.SSS2" title="2.2.2 Parallel and Sequential Recursion ‣ 2.2 Task-Level Recursion ‣ 2 Harness2 ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2.2</span></a></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/o library</em> improves each task as before
but neither reads from nor writes to the improvement library, so no task benefits from
what earlier ones tried. <em id="S4.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/o scoping</em> replaces the invariant and domain
editors with two generic ones, so the same number of candidates is drafted
from the same evidence and probed under the same budget, but neither reads
the trajectory at a stated scope. <em id="S4.p6.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/o composition</em> probes both
candidates and then skips composition, returning whichever the evidence
favours, so the two proposals remain alternatives rather than parts.
Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4 Analysis ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows that removing the library lowers
WorkBuddy-Bench and JobBench scores by <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8</annotation></semantics></math> points,
respectively; removing scoping costs <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.9</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.7</annotation></semantics></math>, and removing
composition costs <math id="S4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.9</annotation></semantics></math>. All three components contribute
to performance. Appendix <a href="#A5.SS1" title="E.1 Contributions of Harness Components ‣ Appendix E Supplementary Experiments and Analyses ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> further evaluates
removing prompt-related components, skills, and scripts from the improved harness.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Analysis of Harnessing-Level Recursion.</span> We investigate whether updating a continual improvement harness enhances subsequent refinement and how this benefit scales with task-level exploration. Figure <a href="#S4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 4 Analysis ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (left) shows that directly refining the base execution harness without access to reference executions, candidate probes, or the improvement library degrades performance on Code and Web. Specifically, Code scores drop from <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="73.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>73.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">73.4</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="63.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>63.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">63.2</annotation></semantics></math> and Web scores fall from <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="69.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>69.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">69.9</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="65.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>65.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">65.0</annotation></semantics></math>. An improvement library accumulated at <math id="S4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}1</annotation></semantics></math> restores base performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F7" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:64%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.14224v1/library_transfer.svg" id="S4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:310/100;" width="310" height="100"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="S4.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Harnessing-level recursion.<span id="S4.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Left: direct refinement with the improvement harness.
Right: JobBench-to-WorkBuddy-Bench library transfer for one-step refinement.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>, the library instead supports gains of <math id="S4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.1</annotation></semantics></math> points on Code, Web, and Office. Greater task-level exploration thus benefits subsequent harnessing without further probing. A JobBench-derived library also improves one-step refinement on WorkBuddy-Bench by <math id="S4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.9</annotation></semantics></math> points, respectively (Figure <a href="#S4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 4 Analysis ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, right). Excluding each task’s own library entry yields gains of <math id="S4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.9</annotation></semantics></math> points on WorkBuddy-Bench and <math id="S4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.7</annotation></semantics></math> on JobBench (Figure <a href="#A5.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ E.2 Reuse of Harnesses and Improvement Experience ‣ Appendix E Supplementary Experiments and Analyses ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). This retrospective test uses later-task experience to evaluate cross-task reuse, not online adaptation. Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Supplementary Experiments and Analyses ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> analyzes component reuse.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2610.14224v1/figures/same_model.png" id="S4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/137;" width="476" height="137" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="S4.F8.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Same model as executor and editor.<span id="S4.F8.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Base harness versus
<span id="S4.F8.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Harness<sup id="S4.F8.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S4.F8.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">2</span></sup></span> with OpenCode at <math id="S4.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}2</annotation></semantics></math>. Annotations show score gains.</span></span></figcaption>
