<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Supplementary Experiments and Analyses</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first examine the contributions of individual harness components and
the reuse of accumulated experience. We then evaluate cross-model
transfer, tool-use reliability, and alternative production harnesses,
before presenting failure analyses and qualitative cases.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Contributions of Harness Components</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We remove prompt-related components, skills, or scripts from the already
improved harness and reevaluate it without rerunning improvement
(Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ E.1 Contributions of Harness Components ‣ Appendix E Supplementary Experiments and Analyses ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). This tests the contribution of
retained components, rather than the ability to compensate for their
absence during improvement.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="A5.T6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value across harness components on WorkBuddy-Bench.</span>
