<div id="A5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No fixed harness leads on every domain: Claude Code performs best on
Code and Office, while Codex leads on Web (Figure <a href="#A5.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ E.5 Comparison with Production Harnesses ‣ Appendix E Supplementary Experiments and Analyses ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).
Starting from OpenCode, <span id="A5.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Harness<sup id="A5.SS5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A5.SS5.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">2</span></sup></span> exceeds the strongest fixed alternative
by <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.6</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.8</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.9</annotation></semantics></math> points on Code, Web, and Office.
The corresponding gains over its own starting harness are <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.4</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A5.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8.4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9.4</annotation></semantics></math> points. This comparison shows the benefit of refining
an existing harness, while noting that refinement uses additional
test-time compute.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.6 </span>Failure Analysis</h3>

<div id="A5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A5.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ E.6 Failure Analysis ‣ Appendix E Supplementary Experiments and Analyses ‣ Harness2: Recursive Agent Harnessing foran Open World" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> groups nine regressions into three
categories. First, selection can prefer a weaker candidate: on
WB-code, an output scoring <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>55</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">55</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen over one scoring <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95</annotation></semantics></math>;
on LAB, narrower coverage reduces the score from <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="54" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>54</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">54</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="26" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>26</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">26</annotation></semantics></math>.
Second, an incorrect premise can propagate across candidates.
A literal-key requirement or an unchecked cache assumption leads
to losses of <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A5.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> points. Third, outcome variability, missing
judge verdicts, and edits that do not address the evaluated criteria
complicate attribution of the remaining regressions.
These cases motivate selection that better balances coverage and
precision, probes that challenge shared assumptions, and repeated
executions to distinguish editing effects from outcome variation.</p>
</div>
